.TH ANONYMARK 1 "October 2026" "anonymark 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anonymark \- pixel-matched screenshot anonymizer and synthetic data replacement engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anonymark
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B anonymark
is a native macOS and Go CLI utility that captures or processes application screenshots and replaces sensitive network and environment identifiers in-place. Using macOS Vision OCR, clustered perimeter background sampling, ink-height typography estimation, and CoreText baseline rendering,
.B anonymark
replaces private IPv4 addresses, hardware MAC addresses, internal hostnames, local filesystem user paths, email addresses, and API tokens without visual cut-out artifacts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B capture
Launch the interactive macOS screen selection overlay (\fBscreencapture -i\fR) and immediately anonymize the captured region.
.TP
.B process \fIinput.png\fR
Anonymize an existing PNG or JPEG screenshot file on disk.
.TP
.B completion \fIzsh|bash\fR
Generate shell completion scripts for Zsh or Bash.
.TP
.B version
Display the installed version of
.BR anonymark .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-out " path"
Output image file path (default: \fIanonymized.png\fR).
.TP
.BI \-mode " mode"
Visual redaction style: \fBsynthetic\fR (default), \fBpill\fR, or \fBblur\fR.
.SH AUTHOR
Mark Sjurseth
